{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"hermitlike-ammonitoid-redpoll","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Operator ruling (2026-08-21, adjudicated on 5bca-4ca9)\nThe LLM import-integrity code-review criterion is DECLINED (8b86-fe08 closed wontfix). The import/packaging-regression class is deterministically measurable, so it gets a deterministic check.\n\n## Problem\nCI's artifact probe (.github/workflows/_artifact-probe.yml) installs the built wheel in a clean venv but only runs 'import rebar', the two entry-point --help calls, and a JSON-resource walk. Escaped regressions this misses: subpackage import breakage (helpers unable to import the git adapter), scripts/ modules that only resolve with scripts/ on sys.path, lazy provider imports broken by monkeypatch-target moves.\n\n## Approach\n- A checked-in script (e.g. scripts/check_import_walk.py) that (1) walks every module under the installed rebar package via pkgutil/importlib and imports each, reporting every failure (not fail-fast on the first); (2) has a scripts/ leg importing each top-level scripts/*.py module under its documented sys.path contract.\n- Wire it into the wheel-probe CI job (runs inside the clean wheel venv) AND keep it locally runnable (make target or direct script run) — the blocking project.portability criterion forbids CI-only triggers.\n- Modules with legitimate import-time side effects or optional-dependency guards get an explicit, documented skip/expected list — additions require a recorded reason.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] The walk imports every rebar.* module in the wheel-probe venv and fails CI on any ImportError, reporting all failures\n- [ ] A scripts/ import leg covers top-level scripts modules under their real sys.path contract\n- [ ] Locally runnable without CI (portability); documented in the doc the wheel probe references\n- [ ] Regression proof: at least one historical escaped case (e.g. bare 'import alert_dedup' sys.path shape) is shown caught by the walk (recreate its pre-fix shape in a test or demonstrate on the historical commit)\n- [ ] Optional-dependency modules ([agents] extra absent) handled: walk passes on the base wheel with the skip-list documented","id":"37b9-fa7e-e10e-4dcc","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Deterministic import walk: import every rebar.* module in the wheel probe + a scripts/ leg"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787356646815436001,"uuid":"8d55acaf-3be1-4d25-9f34-b20ef55dd88b"}